        "text": "Cognition states that SWE-2 Flash runs at one-fifth the price of SWE-2, and that SWE-2 list price is 3.00 dollars per 1M input tokens, 15.00 dollars per 1M output tokens, and 0.30 dollars per 1M cache-input tokens. Cognition has not published a standalone per-token line item for SWE-2 Flash: the model does not appear anywhere in the Devin documentation index, the Devin models page, or the Devin API reference as of November 5, 2026. Treat the one-fifth figure as a vendor claim rather than a published rate. The launch post also advertises SWE-2 Flash as free through November 30, 2026."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you call SWE-2 Flash through an API?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not as a normal per-token API. Cognition's launch post says SWE-2 Flash is available in Devin Desktop and Devin CLI. The Devin v3 session API accepts a devin_mode parameter whose documented values are normal, fast, fusion, lite, ultra, swe-2-medium, swe-2-high, and swe-2-max, with no swe-2-flash value, and the Devin models page lists SWE-2, SWE-1.7, SWE-1.7 Lightning, SWE-1.6, SWE-1.6 Fast, SWE-1-mini, swe-grep, and swe-check, with no SWE-2 Flash entry. Access is therefore through Devin product surfaces rather than a standalone inference endpoint."
      }
