        "text": "Only sometimes. Cognition's published comparison table shows SWE-2 Flash at 24.0 on FrontierCode 2.0 against SWE-2 at 23.8, and near-ties on SWE-Bench Pro v2 Hard at 89.9 versus 90.6. On the other measures the larger sibling wins: Terminal-Bench 4.0 at 27.3 versus 20.0, DeepSWE 1.1 at 73.0 versus 60.1, SWE-Atlas QA at 56.3 versus 50.0, and Terminal-Bench 2.1 at 92.8 versus 89.2. SWE-2 Flash is smaller and cheaper, not uniformly stronger."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is SWE-2 Flash cheaper than open API coding models?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "On the implied one-fifth-of-SWE-2 rate, no. SWE-2 list pricing is 3.00 dollars input and 15.00 dollars output per 1M tokens, so one fifth would be roughly 0.60 dollars input and 3.00 dollars output. OpenRouter route prices checked on November 5, 2026 list GLM 5.3 Flash at 0.15 dollars input and 0.50 dollars output, DeepSeek V4.1 Flash at 0.045 dollars input and 0.50 dollars output, GPT-6 Luna at 0.10 dollars and 0.50 dollars, and Claude Haiku 5.5 at 0.10 dollars and 0.50 dollars. On a 10K input and 40K output turn, the implied SWE-2 Flash rate costs roughly six times DeepSeek V4.1 Flash."
      }
